sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as Clinical User
    participant W as Enterprise WeCom
    participant G as WeCom Gateway
    participant C as Conversation Center
    participant I as Service Intake
    participant T as Unified Ticket Core
    participant O as Communication Outbox
    participant A as AI Provider (optional)
    participant H as Human Workbench

    U->>W: Text / image / file
    W->>G: WebSocket Frame
    G->>I: Normalized Message
    I->>I: Persist Channel Message and Intake idempotently
    I->>T: Create Ticket when service work is required
    T->>T: Ticket + Event + Outbox in one transaction
    T-->>G: Ticket number / truthful acknowledgement
    G-->>W: Reply after commit
    W-->>U: Visible acknowledgement

    I-->>C: Project committed message into Thread / Session
    C-->>H: Realtime event via SSE
    H->>C: Human takeover / reply command
    C->>O: Commit external message and delivery intent
    O->>G: Reliable delivery
    G->>W: Active send

    C--)A: Redacted context, generation_version N
    A-->>C: Suggestion / draft
    C->>C: Verify generation_version and safety
    alt stale or human takeover
        C->>C: Save AI Run as STALE; do not send
    else approved external reply
        C->>O: Commit AI message and delivery intent
    end

    Note over T,O: Unified Ticket Core remains authoritative
    Note over C,A: AI failure never blocks human-only flow
